# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"
msgstr "Operator backpropagation {#operator-backpropagation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements operator backpropagation (OBP) for reducing depth of circuits in expectation value calculations. This technique propagates an observable backward through gates at the end of a quantum circuit, which results in a more shallow circuit at the cost of an increase in observable measurement bases. As one backpropagates an operator further through a circuit, the size of the observable grows exponentially, resulting in both a classical and quantum resource overhead. However, for some circuits, the resulting distribution of Pauli observables is more concentrated than the worst-case exponential scaling, meaning that some terms in the Hamiltonian with small coefficients can be truncated to reduce the quantum overhead. The error incurred by doing this can be controlled to find a suitable tradeoff between precision and efficiency.\n"
msgstr "Pakej ini melaksanakan operator backpropagation (OBP) untuk mengurangkan kedalaman litar dalam pengiraan nilai jangkaan. Teknik ini merambatkan observable ke belakang melalui gate di hujung litar kuantum, yang menghasilkan litar yang lebih cetek dengan kos peningkatan asas pengukuran observable. Apabila operator dibackpropagate lebih jauh melalui litar, saiz observable bertambah secara eksponen, menyebabkan overhed sumber klasik dan kuantum. Walau bagaimanapun, bagi sesetengah litar, taburan observable Pauli yang terhasil lebih tertumpu daripada penskalaan eksponen kes terburuk, bermakna sesetengah sebutan dalam Hamiltonian dengan pekali kecil boleh dipangkas untuk mengurangkan overhed kuantum. Ralat yang ditanggung akibat tindakan ini boleh dikawal untuk mencari pertukaran yang sesuai antara ketepatan dan kecekapan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are a number of ways in which operator backpropagation can be performed, this package uses a method based on Clifford perturbation theory, which has the benefit that the overhead incurred by backpropagating various gates is determined by the non-Cliffordness of that gate. This leads to an increased efficiency for some families of circuits relative to tensor-network based methods for OBP, which currently have high classical overheads even in cases where the quantum overhead remains tame.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat beberapa cara operator backpropagation boleh dilakukan; pakej ini menggunakan kaedah berdasarkan teori usikan Clifford, yang mempunyai kelebihan bahawa overhed yang ditanggung oleh backpropagation pelbagai gate ditentukan oleh sifat bukan-Clifford gate tersebut. Ini membawa kepada kecekapan yang lebih tinggi bagi sesetengah keluarga litar berbanding kaedah OBP berasaskan tensor-network, yang pada masa ini mempunyai overhed klasik yang tinggi walaupun dalam kes di mana overhed kuantum kekal terkawal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package is suitable for estimating expectation values of general quantum circuits and Pauli observables; however, for high-magic (very non-Clifford) circuits the observable error incurred from truncation will likely become prohibitive before the observable has been propagated through a meaningful portion of the circuit. For near-Clifford circuits, it may be possible to propagate through much more of the circuit while maintaining relatively small error bounds.\n"
msgstr "Pakej ini sesuai untuk menganggar nilai jangkaan litar kuantum am dan observable Pauli; walau bagaimanapun, bagi litar magic tinggi (sangat bukan-Clifford), ralat observable yang ditanggung daripada pemangkasan berkemungkinan menjadi terlalu tinggi sebelum observable dirambat melalui bahagian litar yang bermakna. Bagi litar hampir-Clifford, mungkin boleh merambat melalui lebih banyak bahagian litar sambil mengekalkan had ralat yang agak kecil.\n"

