# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use case examples {#use-case-examples}"
msgstr "Contoh kes penggunaan {#use-case-examples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This technique has been used to implement lower-depth Trotter circuits for the time-evolution of a 2D spin model [\\[1\\]](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41534-026-01196-0).\n"
msgstr "Teknik ini telah digunakan untuk melaksanakan litar Trotter berkedalaman lebih rendah bagi evolusi masa model spin 2D [\\[1\\]](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41534-026-01196-0).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Technical discussion {#technical-discussion}"
msgstr "Perbincangan teknikal {#technical-discussion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A single entry point:** the `backpropagate` function performs OBP.\n"
msgstr "**Satu titik masuk:** fungsi `backpropagate` melaksanakan OBP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two independent controls over the depth ↔ accuracy tradeoff:**\n"
msgstr "**Dua kawalan bebas ke atas pertukaran kedalaman ↔ ketepatan:**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`OperatorBudget` bounds how large the observable may grow during backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "`OperatorBudget` menghadkan seberapa besar observable boleh membesar semasa backpropagation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`TruncationErrorBudget` bounds how much error may be incurred during backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "`TruncationErrorBudget` menghadkan berapa banyak ralat yang boleh ditanggung semasa backpropagation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Effectiveness depends on how Clifford the circuit is:** for high-magic circuits (i.e. very non-Clifford), terms added to the observable tend to have larger coefficients, so one incurs more truncation error earlier, limiting the depth savings under a fixed error budget. Near-Clifford circuits can be truncated more aggressively and backpropagated deeper under the same budget.\n"
msgstr "**Keberkesanan bergantung pada sejauh mana litar itu Clifford:** bagi litar magic tinggi (iaitu sangat bukan-Clifford), sebutan yang ditambah kepada observable cenderung mempunyai pekali yang lebih besar, jadi ralat pemangkasan yang ditanggung lebih awal lebih banyak, mengehadkan penjimatan kedalaman di bawah bajet ralat tetap. Litar hampir-Clifford boleh dipangkas dengan lebih agresif dan dibackpropagate lebih dalam di bawah bajet yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Fully introspectable:** each run returns an `OBPMetadata` object recording per-slice Pauli counts, QWC-group counts, and accumulated truncation error, with `plot_*` helpers to visualize operator growth and error against circuit depth — useful for tuning budgets before committing QPU time.\n"
msgstr "**Boleh diselidik sepenuhnya:** setiap larian memulangkan objek `OBPMetadata` yang merekodkan bilangan Pauli bagi setiap slice, bilangan kumpulan QWC dan ralat pemangkasan terkumpul, dengan pembantu `plot_*` untuk menggambarkan pertumbuhan operator dan ralat berbanding kedalaman litar — berguna untuk melaras bajet sebelum menggunakan masa QPU.\n"

